  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Timor-Leste continues to face persistent challenges related to informal employment, limited labour protections, and the socio-economic impacts of climate change. A significant portion of the workforce remains engaged in informal jobs, often without access to social protection or legal rights. In this context, trade unions play a crucial role in advocating for a just and equitable transition to a green economy&#x2014;one that upholds workers&apos; rights, promotes inclusive social dialogue, and supports the formalization of employment.
To address these challenges, strengthening national mechanisms that support the transition to formal employment and promote a just transition is considered essential. During this biennium, the ILO supports the Timor-Leste Trade Union Confederation (KSTL) in developing a digital grievance monitoring system for workers, as well as a strategic plan and action programme to guide the transition to formality. These initiatives also contribute to building effective, dialogue-driven frameworks for transitioning to a greener economy and expanding formal employment. The overall aim is to foster inclusive growth, increase formality, and enhance climate resilience&#x2014;particularly for vulnerable populations.</narrative>
  </description>
